  "answer": "The Voyager paper did not fine-tune a policy network and did not use any training hours or GPU hardware for training [C1, C9]. \n\nInstead, Voyager operates completely gradient-free by querying blackbox LLM APIs (specifically OpenAI's `gpt-4-0314`, `gpt-3.5-turbo-0301`, and `text-embedding-ada-002`), which bypasses the need for model parameter fine-tuning [C1, C2, C9]. The system generates executable JavaScript code via prompting to control the agent in MineDojo through Mineflayer APIs rather than executing or optimizing neural policy weights [C2, C8, C9]. Consequently, no training hardware or training durations are reported in the paper [C1, C2, C9]."
